  "finalText": "# Final Answer: Open RMA Processing Complete\n\nBased on the worker report, the return authorizations have been processed as follows:\n\n## Summary of Actions\n\n**12 RMAs Fully Settled and Closed:**\n- Total refunded to cards: 66,675¢\n- Total refunded as store credit: 66,895¢ (applied to customer accounts)\n- Total units restocked: 19 units (11 to sellable stock, 8 to damaged bucket)\n\nRefunds were calculated in accordance with the return policy, applying the 15% restocking fee for \"changed_mind\" returns and no fee for defective/damaged goods. Store credit was issued for returns outside the 30-day window; card refunds for those within it.\n\n**1 RMA Referred for Investigation (RMA-808):**\n- Warehouse received wrong product (cable instead of monitor)\n- Investigation opened per policy: no refund or restock until resolved\n\n**3 RMAs Correctly Left Open:**\n- RMA-807, RMA-809, RMA-816: Units still in transit or pending warehouse receipt\n- Closing these would violate the rule that \"nothing is refunded or restocked for units that have not arrived\"\n\n## Compliance\n\nThe report indicates all actions align with the domain policy: settled returns were refunded and restocked only for units the warehouse received, refunds did not exceed amounts paid, and returns outside the 30-day window were paid as store credit rather than to the original payment method.\n\nThe task appears complete as reported: ready returns have been settled; those awaiting receipt or requiring investigation remain appropriately open.",
